            <ArticleTitle>False aortic aneurysm presenting as sciatic nerve root pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>214-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Neurological symptoms and signs are rarely the only presenting feature of abdominal aortic aneurysm. We present a patient presenting with sciatic nerve root pain due to a large false aneurysm in iliopsoas.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
